# Workflow

- `main` is protected. Open a pull request. Do not merge it. Do not
  `git push --force`, `git push origin main`, or `git reset --hard` on `main`.
- Branch: `<agent>/<issue_number>_<slug>`. Comment `claim` and add
  `in-progress` before editing. One issue, one branch, one pull request.
  Stay inside the issue's file scope.
- Commit messages: `type(scope): summary`. Scope is one of `task`, `verify`,
  `reference`, `taskfmt`, `tooling`, `docs`, `ci`, `deps`, `spec`.
- Pull request sections: issue link, spec reference (`spec/...#anchor`),
  contract changes (or "none" plus an ADR link), the state each claim reached,
  local `make check` output, what is not verified, open science questions.
- Aim under 400 changed lines excluding `data/` and lockfiles.
- Rebase on `main` before review. The owner squash-merges.
- `make check` must pass before the work is called done. Paste the output.
  The stop hook runs the same target.
- Hooks deny edits under `spec/` and `data/gold/`. Read those files. Do not
  write them. Point the denial at the `needs-science-decision` issue flow.
- Update `PROGRESS.md` when a milestone or task status changes.
